From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:21:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: Don't present to a minimised window.

Present1 asked the minimised window's layer for a drawable every frame,
which may block or return none; a game whose fullscreen window was
minimised in the background (the previous commit) keeps rendering. Skip
the present as D3D11 does for an occluded window, returning S_OK (a flip
model swapchain never gets DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED), but rotate the back
buffers and release the frame latency object as a present would, or a
game waiting on it would stall after its latency's worth of frames. A
60 Hz sleep stands in for the drawable's pacing. DXMT_STATS counts the
skipped presents.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp b/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp
index 8f455d4..c19eb51 100644
--- a/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d12/d3d12_swapchain.cpp
@@ -755,6 +755,18 @@ public:
     if (PresentFlags & DXGI_PRESENT_TEST)
       return hr;
 
+    // MacNeutron: a minimised window's layer gets no drawable worth waiting for: skip the present, as D3D11 does for
+    // an occluded window, but return S_OK (flip model never gets DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED), rotate the buffers and free
+    // the frame latency object's slot as a present would. ponytail: a 60 Hz sleep keeps a minimised game from
+    // spinning without the drawable's pacing; the display's refresh rate if 60 Hz is ever too slow.
+    if (wsi::isMinimized(hWnd)) {
+      DXMT_STAT_COUNT("#presents skipped (window minimised)", 1);
+      ReleaseSemaphore(present_semaphore_, 1, nullptr);
+      presentation_count_ += 1;
+      Sleep(16);
+      return hr;
+    }
+
     double vsync_duration = std::max(
         SyncInterval * 1.0 / (preferred_max_frame_rate ? preferred_max_frame_rate : init_refresh_rate_),
         preferred_max_frame_rate ? 1.0 / preferred_max_frame_rate : 0
